From: Kavan Smith <kavansmith82@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: don't re-lock the PHY PLL on every DSI command

Backlight DCS writes during video scanout call msm_dsi_host_xfer_prepare(),
which unconditionally re-runs link_clk_set_rate(). That re-locks the DSI PHY
PLL while the panel is actively displaying, glitching the byte clock and
corrupting the DSC stream (花屏 / black screen on Q706F).

The link rate is already programmed in msm_dsi_host_power_on(); skip the
redundant set once the link is up.

Link: https://lists.freedesktop.org/archives/dri-devel/2018-April/172218.html
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -2114,7 +2114,15 @@
 	 * mdp clock need to be enabled to receive dsi interrupt
 	 */
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(&msm_host->pdev->dev);
-	cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
+	/*
+	 * Don't re-set the link clock rate when the link is already up. The
+	 * requested byte-clock rate rarely equals the DSI PHY PLL's achievable
+	 * rate, so clk_set_rate() re-locks the PLL on every command; for a
+	 * video-mode panel that clock glitch makes the panel lose pixel lock
+	 * mid-scanout (e.g. every backlight update).
+	 */
+	if (!msm_host->power_on)
+		cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
 	cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_enable(msm_host);
 
 	/* TODO: vote for bus bandwidth */
